A||||12||Cheever2||Had a good trip to the FCO FieroFest||||10||
Z||000000||Cheever2||05-21-2001||04:14 PM||||I'm all smiles, since after entering my first show I won my class.  Sure there weren't as many entries as Carlisle or Daytona but the experience showed me that hard work pays off.<P>I got off work at midnight Friday night, went home to finish packing, and attach stimpy's decklid for the trip.  Me & Tim (13) got on the road at 2:00 am.  We arrived at 9:30, took off the decklid, introduced ourselves, then ran out to the car wash.  I never did so much cleaning to any car before, and certainly not so quickly.  We got back and the judging was underway, barely got our bags out of the trunk in time to get out of the judges' way.  Only then did me & the kid have time to walk around and see the other cars, including a Mera and some V-8's.  Will finish the film & get it to PhotoWorks asap.  Yes, Cliff, there should be one of me with the T-shirt transfer!  Later we went with Mr & Mrs stimpy and friend (Doug, I think) for lunch to their favorite Mexican place, which had great food & service and live music.  We went to see the air conditioner I'm considering buying to cool my garage.  Then after checking into the Days Inn it was time to meet up at the park where there was even more food.  Both of us left early cause we were running out of steam, but on the way out I noticed a coupe with a Power Tour 2001 sticker - did that belong to Pontiacs4me, by chance?  Got to sleep at 6:00 pm while my kid watched TV, woke up at 2:00 to a strong storm.  Turned on the Weather Channel but the lightening knocked it out for a few seconds.  Finally got more sleep.<P>Sunday we took Route 66 to Tulsa.  It's still a great road, lots of fun for a Fiero.  Had lunch with my parents and brother, met Fiero owner Patrick Spreng who does Whoopi Goldberg's website.  He has a decent 86 GT.  His son Evan was with him.  Nice folks, but we didn't get to talk much.<P>On the way home we discovered the Expedia.com driving directions led us astray, and we had to be creative.  We had fun on the backroads all the same, and waved at a perfect red 88 GT going the other way.  He waved back, too.  Got gas out of some old gas pumps like I hadn't seen in many years.  Made it home at midnight.  <P>Great memories for me and my son.  The wonderful people we met at the show proved once again that Fiero folks are the best.  Like stimpy said in another post, next year's 10th Annual will be a terrific event.  Hope lots of people come.  I'll be back with Expeditor (my GT).||||reg||10
Z||000001||stimpy||05-21-2001||04:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>Later we went with Mr & Mrs stimpy for lunch to their favorite Mexican place, which had great food & service and live music. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Mr. & Mrs. stimpy knows how to eat! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It was really cool to see you ther. I hope 2002 brings a lot more folks from out of state to take to lunch.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||T-top Fiero||05-21-2001||08:04 PM||||Congratulations on your win. Did they have any awards to give out at the awards ceremony this year? Last year no one knew what the official results were until a couple of days later and on top of that there weren't any awards purchased yet to give out. I had to wait well over a month until they were finally mailed out. <P>Still a little miffed about my experience there last year.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||05-21-2001||09:15 PM||||T-top: During the awards ceremony they announced that they blew it last year, tried to do better this year, and will start planning now for doing a really good production next year.  I had not heard about last year's problems until then.  Yes, they had plaques which look pretty good IMO, and the awards were given out very promptly once the judging was completed.  Their biggest problem was getting us participants to stop walking around talking, and come to the tables to hear the presentations.<P>Keep in mind this was intended to be an informal event, with no strict regimen stating exactly when you must register or when the judging will begin & end or where you must stand, etc.  I knew from the beginning that the focus was on having fun and enjoying the comaraderie, and that's exactly what I got out of it.  Which made an excellent impression on my kid's view of what Fiero car shows are all about.  ||||reg||6
Z||000004||T-top Fiero||05-21-2001||10:18 PM||||Glad to hear that things were a little more prepared for this year. I had a good time last year, but didn't care for the lack of preparation and honesty from the club. Maybe we will see each other there next year. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||05-21-2001||10:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by T-top Fiero:<BR><B>Still a little miffed about my experience there last year. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Can't blame you, really. My impression of last year was that it was a major cluster ferk. There definately are some things that I would still love to see addressed, and I am prepared to make waves if necessary to make some changes that will make no. 10 an even to remember.  I would also love to participate in the North Texas clubs events. Do y'all ever have any? Funny that I haven't heard of anything happening down there...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||curtis||05-23-2001||12:24 AM||||Hey Stimpy, I've been in the North Texas Fiero club about a year and half. We really just meet every 4th saturday of the month. I would like for us to do something like the Fiero fest. It's alot of fun to meet other Fiero owners outside of north texas area.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||05-23-2001||10:17 AM||||Curtis, it was really cool meeting ou and your brother. We really appreciate when people come way out of their way to show up. I would really like to attend a Texas event, maybe you could inspire your fellow club members to put a little on the line and get a Dallas show going. <P>BTW, am I just over sensitive? This just bugs me more and more each time I see it...<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by T-top Fiero:<BR><B> I had a good time last year, but didn't care for the lack of honesty from the club. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>There definately was a lack of planning last year, and certain members who took on resposibilities dropped the ball. I don't think that equates FCO as a bunch of liars. I think that is a low blow. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||05-23-2001||10:31 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR>I would really like to attend a Texas event<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Don't forget the Roundup_5 in San Antonio, June 30 & July 1. <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners&naventryid=110" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners&naventryid=110</A>   <BR>What?  You're not afraid of a little drive, are ya? (j/k)  I can't be there, have to work & can't get out of it.<P>Me & 2 others from Lone Star Fieros will be in the Bud Classic in Houston on June 9th.  This is for all makes.  Wish me luck.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||T-top Fiero||05-23-2001||10:24 PM||||Stimpy, I guess it wasn't right for me to call the whole club dishonest. The main problem I had was with Gary. I see things were better this year.<BR>As far as The North Texas Fiero's, no one in our club has enough initiative to set up a Fiero car show locally.(Myself included) We do go to some local car shows. June 8,9 & 10 we have the Pontiac Southern Nationals here in Dallas and some of us are going to the Fiero Round Up in San Antonio at the end of June.||||reg||1
Z||000010||curtis||05-23-2001||11:25 PM||||Hey T-Top, where abouts do you live in Dallas. I'm in Cedar Hill. Are you going to the meeting this sat?||||reg||5
